    "details": {
      "alignment": "Unaligned",
      "type": {
        "value": "construct",
        "subtype": "Fawful-Bot"
      },
      "cr": 1,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Fawful's Forces packet sheet — Intake Drone.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-forge-packets.py</code> from the NPC Forge roster <code>data/forge/fawfuls-forces.json</code> (entry <code>intake-drone</code>): Small construct (Fawful-Bot), Unaligned; CR 1 (proficiency +2, to hit +4 with DEX); AC 13 (brass shell), hit points 27 (6d6+6), speed 10 ft., fly 40 ft. (hover). A GM scene kit for the Fawful's Forces article's present (1040 BF), not a filed event; the faction article stays the authority.</p><p>The vacuum intake is the oldest trick in the Beanish playbook — the 1035 BF record has it on the head of Fawful's own double — and the Intake Drone is that trick given rotors. It drifts along the castle's ceilings, hums, and then hauls whatever it fancies ten feet across the floor and into the funnel. The occupation uses them as retrievers: a drone brings the Countess a prisoner the way a dog brings a stick.</p><p>Fight it like a grab, not a monster. The pull is the whole statblock; break the grapple, or jam the funnel with a helmet, a chair leg, a Chortle-Bot, and it wheezes and backs off for a turn. Rangers and anyone with a reach weapon do well against them; anyone fighting on a balcony does not.</p><p><strong>Role:</strong> flying grabber · <strong>tier:</strong> Fawful-Bot · <strong>folder:</strong> Fawful's Furious Freaks / Machines of Fury.</p><h3>Art</h3><p>Token plate <code>portraits/fawfuls-forces/intake-drone.png</code> — NPC Forge render, seed 410002, cut from a flat #FF00FF field. Prompt: <q>Clean cel-shaded cartoon character art in the style of Mario & Luigi RPG concept art, bold dark outlines, flat colours, simple shading. A round brass and olive-green flying robot with a huge dark vacuum funnel for a mouth, a single red glowing lens eye, four small propeller rotors on brass arms, and crackling blue electricity under it instead of legs. Full body, whole figure visible, three-quarter view, centred, isolated on a plain flat solid magenta background (#FF00FF), no floor, no ground shadow, no text, no border.</q></p>",
        "public": ""
      }
    },
